ed pre-existing).\\nLint and typescript checks are green.\\n\\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for vitest config aliases\\n\\nnew URL('./path', import.meta.url).pathname returns /C:/Users/... on\\nWindows, which is not a valid filesystem path for Node's fs or\\npath.resolve. The seven alias replacements in vitest.config.ts all\\nrelied on .pathname, so the test suite would have silently broken for\\nWindows contributors.\\n\\nAdd a small helper that wraps fileURLToPath so each call site stays\\nreadable, and route every URL-based path through it.\\n\\nAlso update tsconfig.json to include vitest.config.ts and drop the\\nstale references to setupTests.ts (the actual file lives under src/)\\nand jest.config.js (deleted in this PR). Without vitest.config.ts in\\nthe include list, typed eslint refuses to lint it.\\n\\n* (chore) Document why specific tests are skipped during vitest migration\\n\\nFive tests / blocks were skipped during the jest-to-vitest migration\\nwithout an inline marker explaining the symptom or who is expected to\\nunskip them. Add a TODO comment above each:\\n\\n- ui-select-extended 'Enter/New mode' and 'Edit mode': the Carbon\\n  UiSelectExtended combobox no longer exposes its options to the\\n  accessible-name queries the tests rely on under jsdom +\\n  @testing-library/react 16.\\n- form-engine 'should evaluate months on ART': the test wired up\\n  jest-fake-timers' doNotFake option, which vitest's fakeTimers API\\n  does not provide a direct equivalent for.\\n- form-engine 'should save diagnosis field on form submission' and\\n  'should edit diagnosis field on form submission': the Carbon\\n  combobox in the diagnosis-search workspace has the same option\\n  discoverability issue as ui-select-extended.\\n\\nNo behaviour change; comments only.\\n\\n* (chore) Move setup-tests.ts out of src/ into tools/\\n\\nPer review feedback: this file is test infrastructure, not library\\nsource, so it doesn't belong under src/. Matches the convention used in\\nother recent PRs in this repo.\\n\\n- src/setup-tests.ts → tools/setup-tests.ts\\n- vitest.config.ts: setupFiles path updated\\n- tsconfig.json: add tools/setup-tests.ts to include (the previous\\n  src/**/* glob picked it up; now it's outside that glob)\\n- package.json: drop the now-redundant \\\"!src/setup-tests.ts\\\" files\\n  exclusion (the file is no longer in src/)\\n\\nThe build script's \\\"--ignore '**/setup-tests.*'\\\" pattern and\\ntsconfig.build.json's exclude pattern still match by basename, so no\\nchange there.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":4}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c8e374f-6e9f-4b78-9042-e4ee8bd8b73a","uuid":"2f6ba357-1cdf-4e82-89e0-9fb2d179e20f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:40:10.515Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c79bf029d7ce3c51921276c656bea05e82780f4b\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T15:47:45+05:30\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) O3-5847: Stop datetime obs shifting a day across timezones (#838)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4db319f4ec64190c6197330675a447dd0121f6df\",\"date\":\"2026-08-14T17:42:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(test) Add scaffolding for better testing (#783)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b99cb4c27946bf936dce89d37baebe31720f8ef8\",\"date\":\"2026-06-11T23:02:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5735: Keep default encounter datetimes within the visit window during retrospective data entry (#756)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2204ac05b44795dec06b132c0d15ca1b010bcd95\",\"date\":\"2026-05-13T16:35:49+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#742)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\\n\\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, 